# Nova main origin — strict SPA security policy (M2; ADR-0001, ADR-0008).
# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format (both use the same syntax).
# GitHub Pages IGNORES this file (it cannot send custom headers; the same
# policy is delivered as a build-time CSP meta tag instead — see
# docs/architecture/deployment.md).
#
# Substitute YOUR real origins before use:
#   - CSP `frame-src`       -> your runtime origin, e.g. https://runtime.nova.example
#   - CSP `frame-ancestors` -> keep 'none' (the main app is never framed)
# When the site uses a Vite base path (project-site layout), prefix the
# paths below with that base (e.g. /nova/assets/*).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' wss: ws:; media-src 'self' blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; frame-src https://runtime.nova.example
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
